              "id": "CVE-2025-13281",
              "name": "LanguageSpecificPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "kube-controller-manager: Portworx Half-Blind SSRF in kube-controller-manager"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A half-blind Server Side Request Forgery (SSRF) vulnerability exists in kube-controller-manager when using the in-tree Portworx StorageClass. This vulnerability allows authorized users to leak arbitrary information from unprotected endpoints in the control plane’s host network (including link-local or loopback services)."
              },
